WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.662
The second set of clocks
is vendor support.

2
00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:07.909
After end of support there are no new
security updates and no assisted support,

3
00:00:07.909 --> 00:00:11.863
and for an estate built in the
early 2000s, the dates cluster.

4
00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:19.524
Windows 10 and Exchange Server 2016 and 2019
ended in October 2025; SQL Server 2016,

5
00:00:19.524 --> 00:00:22.566
SharePoint Server 2016 and 2019,

6
00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:28.763
and the last Windows Server 2012
security updates ended this year.

7
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:33.907
Windows Server 2016 ends on January
12, 2027, under three months away,

8
00:00:33.907 --> 00:00:40.062
and it's the operating system of many domain
controllers built in the last decade.

9
00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:48.349
Windows Server 2019 and Microsoft Identity
Manager 2016 end on January 9, 2029.

10
00:00:48.349 --> 00:00:51.859
Identity Manager's date
was extended from 2026,

11
00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:57.438
so an agency that syncs HR data through
it has a date, not an open-ended bridge.

12
00:00:57.438 --> 00:01:01.763
A vendor date isn't a federal mandate
on its own, but the two connect.

13
00:01:01.763 --> 00:01:07.197
BOD 26-02 turns end of support into a
directed action for internet-facing edge

14
00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:10.932
devices, and every system
security plan asserts flaw

15
00:01:10.932 --> 00:01:14.838
remediation that an unsupported
product can't deliver.

16
00:01:14.838 --> 00:01:17.538
So running past end of
support is a decision,

17
00:01:17.538 --> 00:01:22.413
and it belongs to the authorizing official,
who has to sign the risk acceptance.

18
00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:27.910
The first of those falls due with
Windows Server 2016, on January 12.
